Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the Ambari Metrics System (AMS) stopping after a Rolling Upgrade (RU) due to issues with the Helix cluster not being fully set up, which prevented the addition of instances to the cluster. The original implementation did not adequately handle scenarios where the cluster was not ready, leading to failures in adding participant instances.

